    "searchCoverage": "Official geocode-api.arcgis.com World GeocodeServer. Auth is the token query parameter (pinned executor); proxy X-Esri-Authorization is not used. Suggests are 0 credits and require authentication, so healthcheck is GET /suggest?text=Berlin&maxSuggestions=1 rather than billed findAddressCandidates/reverseGeocode. HTTP 200 bodies with an error object are demoted via bodyErrorPaths [error]. Nested location objects are omitted because native cannot serialize {longitude,latitude} to lon,lat; reverse geocode binds longitude/latitude as location={{longitude}},{{latitude}}. April 2026 developer-credential CVEs were patched 2026-04-13 and are recorded as historical remediated product issues, not an unresolved geocode-API compromise.",
    "incidents": [
      "2026-04-13 Esri April 2026 ArcGIS Security Bulletin: developer-credential privilege issues affecting ArcGIS Online / Location Platform / Enterprise were patched the same day (CVE-2026-33518/33519 on Portal). Historical remediated product vulnerability; not treated as an unresolved geocode-service customer-account compromise under the 2026-09-13 waiver."
    ],
    "remainingGates": [
      "live authentication unverified"
    ],
    "waiverAuthority": "User waiver dated 2026-09-13 permits historical non-China incident coverage."
  },
